lz5-ex v1.5.2 (tag v1.5.2, commit 1bcccdd, 2026-10-09), from
https://github.com/YadeWira/lz5-ex (a fork of LZ5 1.5 by Yann Collet and Przemyslaw
Skibinski). BSD 2-Clause, see LICENSE. Files copied unmodified from lib/: lz5.c,
lz5hc.c, lz5.h, lz5hc.h, lz5common.h, mem.h. zpaq-std 65.4m-pre56 and pre57 used
lz5-ex commit 5541227; up to pre55 these were LZ5 1.5 (tag v1.5 of
inikep/lizard), byte for byte.

Same block format as LZ5 1.5, so the ZPAQLZ5 decoder in every -ma:lz5 block is
unchanged and archives of both versions extract with both. Compared with LZ5 1.5:
- HC levels 2 and 4 to 10 write blocks 0.5-0.9% smaller, levels 1, 3 and 11 within
  0.2% of LZ5 1.5 (measured on 96 MB of mixed data); lz5f, lz5:1-4 and HC 12-15
  write the same bytes;
- the decoder checks match offsets by distance instead of comparing pointers;
- LZ5_decompress_safe no longer reads past the end of its input, and the HC match
  finder no longer reads past the end of the data; neither showed in zpaq-std,
  whose buffers have spare capacity, but both were real;
- the compressor never writes past maxDstSize. zpaq-std passes the original size
  minus 17, which LZ5 1.5 already honoured.
Do not patch these files here: send changes to the lz5-ex repository.
